# CASE STUDY: Autonomous Real Estate Outbound & Pocket Listing Intelligence Engine (Dubai)

> **Architect & Engineer:** Aleksandr Krupenko  
> **Domain:** Dubai Secondary Real Estate / PropTech / GTM & Sales Operations Automation  
> **Engineering Standard:** C.R.E.S.T. Framework (Critical Analysis, Resilience, Ergonomics, Security, Throughput)  
> **Infrastructure Cost:** **$6/month Total** (Single 1 GB RAM VPS), $0/mo in SaaS and paid messaging APIs

---

## 1. Executive Summary & Core Broker Pain Point

In the competitive Dubai secondary real estate market, particularly for individual brokers and agents building their property pipeline, the single biggest bottleneck is **cold calling property owner databases**. 

* **The Problem:** Manual cold calling requires dozens of hours weekly, suffers from extremely low connection rates, high burn-out, and slow coverage.
* **The Solution:** An autonomous, event-driven engine designed to fully replace manual cold calling. The system validates contact databases, dispatches personalized initial outreach via WhatsApp, qualifies inbound responses using LLM-driven NLU, and automatically feeds confirmed properties into a live **Pocket Listing**.
* **Pocket Listing Strategy (Agent-to-Agent Revenue):** Instead of noisy chat alerts, high-intent leads are written directly to a structured Google Sheet (Pocket Listing). This live portfolio is shared with co-brokering networks—matching private property inventory directly with buyers' agents to drastically increase transaction velocity.

