## 3. Key Workflows Breakdown & Functional Design

### 1. Database Validation (`WA Number Validation`)
Before any outreach campaign runs, contacts pass through an automated validation loop (`Loop Over Items` with a 7-second rate-limit buffer)[cite: 3]. Non-WhatsApp numbers are tagged and filtered out in Supabase prior to sequence dispatch to prevent API waste and reduce anti-spam triggers[cite: 3].

### 2. Autonomous Outbound Dispatcher (`Outbound Workflow`)
Replaces manual phone calls[cite: 4]. Scheduled cron triggers pull queued leads from Supabase, verify active business hours (Dubai GST time), format personalized messages with dynamic property details, and route them through Evolution API[cite: 4].

### 3. Inbound NLU & Pocket Listing Pipeline (`Inbound Workflow`)
Incoming WhatsApp replies hit a dedicated Webhook and are instantly processed by Gemini API[cite: 5]:
* **Direct Agent Interaction:** Since incoming WhatsApp messages appear directly on the broker's phone, duplicate Telegram lead alerts were intentionally omitted to prevent notification fatigue.
* **Pocket Listing Automation:** When a property owner confirms interest (`INTERESTED`), the system updates PostgreSQL and automatically writes the validated property parameters to a master **Google Sheet**[cite: 5]. This sheet acts as a real-time **Pocket Listing**, immediately ready for B2B sharing with co-brokerage agents who have active buyers.
* **Auto-Opt-Out:** Negative responses (`REJECTED`) or competitor replies (`AGENT`) automatically flag the record in PostgreSQL to halt further communication[cite: 5].

### 4. End-to-End Performance Analytics (`Analytics - Weekly Performance Report` / `Market Analytics Catcher`)
A dedicated monitoring workflow queries PostgreSQL to evaluate system health and campaign performance[cite: 2]:
* Tracks total numbers processed vs. active WhatsApp delivery rate[cite: 2].
* Measures exact conversion percentages: Outreach Volume $\rightarrow$ Delivery $\rightarrow$ Positive Owner Replies (`INTERESTED`) vs. Opt-outs (`REJECTED`)[cite: 2].
* Provides data-backed insights to continuously optimize message copy, timing, and database targeting[cite: 2].

### 5. Centralized Error Catcher (`System - Global Error Handler`)
A global exception workflow monitoring all 6 micro-services[cite: 2]. Network drops or API timeouts automatically trigger a rich diagnostic alert (`Workflow Name`, `Node Name`, `Error Message`, `Execution ID`) sent directly to an internal Telegram ops chat for immediate troubleshooting[cite: 2].

